{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findingId\":\"finding-001\",\"hypothesisId\":\"finding-001-canary-h1\",\"baselineSha256\":\"8156259e4652d73265445dae77bebbd2b82907447d5c23dbcb2b5d4e95dff2d6\",\"revisedContent\":\"## Purpose\\nDetermine whether a strict worker transcript is isolated by detecting executable tool activity, inherited user context, and malformed transport. The procedure protects measurements from workers that use prohibited tools, receive hook, installed-skill, or plugin context, or emit a transcript the supervisor cannot parse reliably.\\n\\n## Inputs\\nReceive the complete raw stdout captured from one worker invocation. The stream may be one JSON document or newline-delimited JSON. Treat every parsed object, nested object, and array item as part of the same transcript. Do not infer events or diagnostics from prose outside the parsed transport.\\n\\n## Procedure\\n1. Parse the whole stream as JSON. If that fails, parse each nonempty line independently and count every line that is not valid JSON.\\n2. Recursively visit all parsed arrays and objects, including nested message and error objects.\\n3. Record an executable tool event when an object's type is tool_use, tool_result, command_execution, mcp_tool_call, web_search, web_search_request, web_fetch, file_search, computer_use, or shell.\\n4. Preserve each recorded event's type and short tool or command name for the receipt.\\n5. Inspect string-valued diagnostic fields in every parsed object. Record hook context when a diagnostic identifies a hook or hooks configuration, including a failure to parse hooks config. Record skill context when a diagnostic states that skills or skill descriptions are installed, visible, loaded, shortened, budgeted, or should be disabled. Record plugin context when a diagnostic states that plugins are installed, visible, loaded, shortened, budgeted, or should be disabled. A single diagnostic may record more than one context class.\\n6. Preserve each context finding's stable class and a short diagnostic excerpt for the receipt.\\n7. Add WORKER_TOOL_CALL when at least one executable tool event was found.\\n8. Add WORKER_HOOK_CONTEXT when at least one hook-context diagnostic was found.\\n9. Add WORKER_SKILL_CONTEXT when at least one skill-context diagnostic was found.\\n10. Add WORKER_PLUGIN_CONTEXT when at least one plugin-context diagnostic was found.\\n11. Add WORKER_TRANSCRIPT_UNPARSEABLE when at least one nonempty transcript line was malformed.\\n12. Fail isolation when any condition is present. Otherwise pass isolation.\\n\\n## Decision Codes\\nA transcript with a recognized executable event is rejected with WORKER_TOOL_CALL. A transcript containing an inherited hook diagnostic is rejected with WORKER_HOOK_CONTEXT. A transcript containing an inherited installed-skill diagnostic is rejected with WORKER_SKILL_CONTEXT. A transcript containing an inherited plugin diagnostic is rejected with WORKER_PLUGIN_CONTEXT. A transcript with malformed nonempty input is rejected with WORKER_TRANSCRIPT_UNPARSEABLE. If multiple conditions occur, retain every applicable reason and reject. A well-formed transcript with zero recognized tool events and zero recognized inherited-context diagnostics is accepted with the canonical code ISOLATION_PASS.\\n\\n## Launch Policy\\nLaunch Codex ephemerally in a read-only capsule, ignore repository instructions, and disable shell, browser, computer-use, multi-agent, hook, plugin, memory, app, goal, tool-suggestion, and workspace-dependency features. The worker receives only the sealed prompt and output schema through the supervisor. Valid JSON error or diagnostic events are not executable tool events, but diagnostics showing inherited hook, installed-skill, or plugin context are isolation failures under this procedure.\\n\\n## Verification\\nReparse the persisted raw stdout rather than trusting the worker packet. Confirm that the stored stdout hash matches the invocation receipt, then apply this procedure. Reproduce the parser outcome, executable-event inventory, inherited-context inventory, malformed-line count, and ordered decision reasons from the sealed raw artifact. The isolation result is valid only when all of them can be reproduced.\",\"changeSummary\":\"Extends strict isolation exactly along the hypothesis: launch-time disabling now covers hook, plugin, memory, app, goal, tool-suggestion, and workspace-dependency features, while recursive transcript inspection rejects inherited hook, installed-skill, and plugin diagnostics with stable WORKER_HOOK_CONTEXT, WORKER_SKILL_CONTEXT, and WORKER_PLUGIN_CONTEXT codes. Existing tool-event, malformed-transport, and clean-pass behavior is preserved.\"}"}}
